  "id": "line-of-beauty",
  "term": "line of beauty",
  "definition": "In this historical aesthetic usage, the line of beauty is a curved, serpentine or waving line that Hogarth treated as the most pleasing kind of outline. Its beauty was linked to the variety in its shape, and he also connected the serpentine form with the phrase line of grace.",
